+# Independent scientific review: Mohr-Coulomb H=0
+
+Decision: **accepted**, 2026-11-02, by actual separate reviewer run `/root/mc_scientific_review`. All nine checklist items pass for the complete selected formulation and the explicitly bounded numerical/interface evidence below. No unresolved scientific transcription blocker was found. This is not a claim that every mathematically admissible input is numerically executable.
+
+Exact definition: `models/mohr-coulomb.json`, SHA-256 `6a3a139218fc413f066abe5b851c5c7aed8899ee23efbd7ae2a2e68c7655f0e5`. Selected source is the two-author Sysala-Cermak arXiv1508.07435v3, constant cohesion, nonassociated three-dimensional perfect plasticity H=0, with Atlas backward Euler, compression-positive effective Cauchy stress and strain, Mandel representation, infinitesimal kinematics and fixed spatial frame/zero spin. The associated subcase psi=phi is included by these equations. No equivalence to the later journal identity is asserted. This review assessed the full model; no source-domain restriction or branch was removed to obtain acceptance.
+
+Independence: this separate dispatched run did not author the existing transcription or its numerical packets. I read the original source, each model expression, source crosswalk, exact-arithmetic branch proof, independent oracle implementation and saved assessments. Historical model-author agent/run IDs are not known; packet task labels are not invented as authenticated run IDs. The schema's nonempty author_run_ids field therefore explicitly records that historical identity is unknown. Prior technical audits are evidence, not substituted scientific reviewers.
+
+## source_provenance
+
+Pass. The actual private PDF exists, has 2,590,234 bytes and SHA-256 `bf35ee09d500b8e21aabdddbdfac363c5f68368f150890c60343bc62447c83ca`. I rendered and visually read complete pages 1 and 7-16, with extracted text for navigation. Page 1 has S. Sysala and M. Cermak, internal date October 15, 2018 and arXiv v3 margin stamp September 27, 2016. Page 7 supplies Eqs3.1-3.6, strict parameter assumptions and admissible H; pp8-13 derive all returns and solvability; pp14-16 supply grouped tensor/tangent expressions and their limitations. Exact original bytes, rather than publication-year inference, govern this review. Original and durable private paths are in the public retention receipt. No web search snippet, abstract or vendor composite law was used in place of governing equations.
+
+## equation_fidelity
+
